Course.start({"num":11,"unit":3,"slug":"m11-verbos-ar","minutes":45,"title":"Los verbos -ar","subtitle":"Regular -ar verbs in the present tense","lede":"Most Spanish verbs end in -ar, and they all follow one pattern. Learn it once and you can use hundreds of verbs.","recap":"In Unit 2 you described people with **ser** and adjectives, and you used possessives like **mi** and **nuestro**. Now you'll talk about what people *do*.","context":{"title":"La rana de Salamanca","place":"Salamanca, España","text":"The **Universidad de Salamanca** was founded in **1218**, which makes it the oldest university in Spain that is still open. For 800 years, students have come here to {{estudiar}}, {{escuchar}} lectures and {{trabajar}} late into the night.\n\nIts stone entrance is covered with carvings of saints, kings and monsters. Hidden among them is a tiny **frog** (*una rana*) sitting on a skull. Tradition says that a student who finds the frog without help will pass every exam. Visitors stand in the plaza for a long time, looking and pointing.\n\nToday thousands of students from around the world come to Salamanca every summer to study Spanish. The first verbs they practice look a lot like the ones in this module: {{Yo estudio. Tú estudias. Nosotros estudiamos.}}"},"learn":[{"title":"Verbs come in three families","text":"The basic form of a verb is the **infinitive**, like *to speak*. In Spanish, every infinitive ends in **-ar**, **-er** or **-ir**. This module is about the biggest family, the **-ar** verbs.\n\nTo use a verb, take off the **-ar** to find the **stem**, then add an **ending** that tells who is doing the action: {{habl**ar**|hablar}} → **habl-** + **o** = {{habl**o**|hablo}} (*I speak*).","flash":[["hablar","to speak, to talk"],["estudiar","to study"],["trabajar","to work"],["escuchar","to listen (to)"],["bailar","to dance"],["cantar","to sing"],["tocar","to play (an instrument), to touch"],["mirar","to look at, to watch"],["necesitar","to need"],["llegar","to arrive"],["tomar","to take, to drink"],["caminar","to walk"]]},{"title":"Six endings: -o, -as, -a, -amos, -áis, -an","text":"Every regular -ar verb uses the same six endings. The ending alone tells you who the subject is, so Spanish speakers often leave out *yo*, *tú* and *nosotros*.","conj":[{"inf":"hablar","en":"to speak","forms":["habl**o**","habl**as**","habl**a**","habl**amos**","habl**áis**","habl**an**"]},{"inf":"estudiar","en":"to study","forms":["estudi**o**","estudi**as**","estudi**a**","estudi**amos**","estudi**áis**","estudi**an**"]}],"examples":[["Hablo inglés y español.","I speak English and Spanish."],["¿Estudias mucho?","Do you study a lot?"],["Mi hermana trabaja los sábados.","My sister works on Saturdays."],["Nosotros escuchamos música.","We listen to music."],["Ustedes bailan muy bien.","You all dance very well."]],"tip":"The **vosotros** form (habl**áis**) is used in Spain for \"you all\" with friends. In Latin America, people use **ustedes** for every \"you all.\" You should recognize both."},{"title":"One verb, three English meanings","text":"{{Hablo español.}} can mean *I speak Spanish*, *I do speak Spanish* or *I am speaking Spanish*. Spanish doesn't need a helper word like *do* or *am*.\n\nTo make a sentence negative, put **no** right before the verb: {{No trabajo los domingos.}} (*I don't work on Sundays.*)\n\nSome verbs already include a word that English adds separately: {{escuchar}} = *to listen **to***, {{mirar}} = *to look **at***, {{buscar}} = *to look **for***. So you say {{Escucho la radio.}}, not *escucho a la radio*.","tip":"When two verbs are together, only the first one changes: {{Necesito estudiar.}} (*I need to study.*)"}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"conj","title":"Conjugate two verbs","intro":"Write all the forms of each verb. Use the endings **-o, -as, -a, -amos, -áis, -an**.","pick":2,"verbs":[{"inf":"trabajar","en":"to work","forms":["trabajo","trabajas","trabaja","trabajamos","trabajáis","trabajan"]},{"inf":"escuchar","en":"to listen","forms":["escucho","escuchas","escucha","escuchamos","escucháis","escuchan"]},{"inf":"bailar","en":"to dance","forms":["bailo","bailas","baila","bailamos","bailáis","bailan"]},{"inf":"cantar","en":"to sing","forms":["canto","cantas","canta","cantamos","cantáis","cantan"]},{"inf":"caminar","en":"to walk","forms":["camino","caminas","camina","caminamos","camináis","caminan"]}],"hints":["Take off **-ar** to find the stem: *trabaj-*, *escuch-*, *bail-*…","Then add the ending for each person: yo **-o**, tú **-as**, él **-a**, nosotros **-amos**, vosotros **-áis**, ellos **-an**.","Only the vosotros form has an accent mark: **-áis**."]},{"id":"t2","type":"select","title":"Choose the right form","intro":"Tap the verb form that matches the subject.","items":[{"s":"Yo {estudio|estudia|estudias} en la biblioteca.","en":"I study in the library."},{"s":"Tú {tocas|toco|tocan} la guitarra.","en":"You play the guitar."},{"s":"La profesora {llega|llegas|llego} a las ocho.","en":"The teacher arrives at eight."},{"s":"Mis amigos y yo {caminamos|caminan|camina} a la escuela.","en":"My friends and I walk to school.","why":"*Mis amigos y yo* = nosotros."},{"s":"Ellas {miran|miramos|mira} la televisión.","en":"They watch television."},{"s":"¿Vosotros {habláis|hablan|hablamos} francés?","en":"Do you all speak French? (Spain)"},{"s":"Ustedes {necesitan|necesitas|necesita} un lápiz.","en":"You all need a pencil.","why":"*Ustedes* uses the same form as *ellos*."},{"s":"Mi papá no {trabaja|trabajo|trabajan} los domingos.","en":"My dad doesn't work on Sundays."}],"hints":["Find the subject first. Who is doing the action?","Two people, one of them *yo*, is always **nosotros** (-amos). *Ustedes* uses the **-an** ending, like *ellos*."]},{"id":"t3","type":"listen","title":"Who is it?","intro":"Listen to each sentence. The subject isn't said, so the **ending** is your only clue. Who is doing the action?","questions":[{"say":"Escuchamos música en el coche.","q":"Who listens to music in the car?","choices":[["nosotros (we)",true,"**-amos** means nosotros."],["ellos (they)",false],["yo (I)",false],["tú (you)",false]]},{"say":"Bailas muy bien.","q":"Who dances very well?","choices":[["tú (you)",true,"**-as** means tú."],["yo (I)",false],["ella (she)",false],["nosotros (we)",false]]},{"say":"Trabajo en un restaurante.","q":"Who works in a restaurant?","choices":[["yo (I)",true,"**-o** means yo."],["él (he)",false],["tú (you)",false],["ellos (they)",false]]},{"say":"Cantan en el coro de la escuela.","q":"Who sings in the school choir?","choices":[["ellos (they)",true,"**-an** means ellos, ellas or ustedes."],["nosotros (we)",false],["yo (I)",false],["usted (you, formal)",false]]},{"say":"Toma el autobús a las siete.","q":"Who takes the bus at seven?","choices":[["él or ella (he or she)",true,"**-a** means él, ella or usted."],["yo (I)",false],["tú (you)",false],["nosotros (we)",false]]}],"hints":["Listen to the very end of the first word.","-o = yo · -as = tú · -a = él/ella/usted · -amos = nosotros · -an = ellos/ellas/ustedes"]},{"id":"t4","type":"cloze","title":"Complete the sentences","intro":"Write the correct form of the verb in parentheses.","items":["Yo [hablo] ((hablar)) con mi abuela por teléfono.","¿Tú [practicas] ((practicar)) deportes después de las clases?","Mi hermano [toca] ((tocar)) el piano.","Nosotros [necesitamos] ((necesitar)) estudiar para el examen.","Los estudiantes [llegan] ((llegar)) temprano.","Usted [trabaja] ((trabajar)) en el hospital, ¿verdad?","Vosotros [cantáis] ((cantar)) en la iglesia.","Tú y Marta [miran] ((mirar)) una película.","Yo no [nado] ((nadar)) en el invierno.","Elena y yo [compramos] ((comprar)) fruta en el mercado."],"pick":8,"hints":["Find the subject, then find the matching ending.","*Tú y Marta* is two people, and one is *you*: that's **ustedes** (-an). *Elena y yo* is **nosotros** (-amos).","Only **-áis** (vosotros) has an accent mark."]},{"id":"t5","type":"order","title":"Build the sentences","intro":"Tap the words in order to translate each sentence. Tap a word in your sentence to send it back. One sentence has a tile that doesn't belong.","items":[{"en":"I listen to music in my room.","es":"Escucho música en mi cuarto.","alt":["Yo escucho música en mi cuarto.","En mi cuarto escucho música."]},{"en":"We don't work on Sundays.","es":"No trabajamos los domingos.","alt":["Los domingos no trabajamos."]},{"en":"Do you dance with your friends?","es":"¿Bailas con tus amigos?","alt":["¿Tú bailas con tus amigos?"]},{"en":"My parents need a new car.","es":"Mis padres necesitan un coche nuevo.","extra":["necesita"]}],"hints":["The verb ending tells who: **-o** yo, **-amos** nosotros, **-as** tú, **-an** ellos.","**No** goes right before the verb.","*Mis padres* is plural, so the verb ends in **-an**. The tile *necesita* doesn't belong."]},{"id":"t6","type":"translate","title":"Say it in Spanish","intro":"Translate each sentence. You can leave out the subject pronoun (*yo*, *tú*, *nosotros*) or include it.","items":[{"en":"I study Spanish.","es":["[yo] estudio español"]},{"en":"She sings very well.","es":["[ella] canta muy bien"]},{"en":"We walk to school.","es":["[nosotros] caminamos a la escuela","[nosotras] caminamos a la escuela"]},{"en":"They don't need a pencil.","es":["[ellos] no necesitan un lápiz","[ellas] no necesitan un lápiz"],"why":"Put **no** before the verb: *no necesitan*."},{"en":"Do you (tú) play the guitar?","es":["¿[tú] tocas la guitarra?"],"why":"*To play an instrument* is **tocar**."}],"hints":["First pick the verb, then the ending for the subject.","*Play an instrument* = **tocar** (not *jugar*). *To school* = **a la escuela**.","*Lápiz* has an accent mark: **lápiz**."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say it out loud","intro":"Listen to each sentence, then record yourself and compare. This is optional, but it helps.","items":[{"s":"Hablo español con mis amigos.","en":"I speak Spanish with my friends."},{"s":"¿Estudias en la biblioteca?","en":"Do you study in the library?"},{"s":"Nosotros caminamos a la escuela.","en":"We walk to school."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Mi semana","prompt":"Write **5 or more sentences** in Spanish about what you, your family and your friends do during a normal week. Use at least **five different -ar verbs**, and at least three different subjects (for example *yo*, *mi mamá*, *mis amigos y yo*).","model":"{{Yo estudio mucho y escucho música por la noche.}} {{Mi mamá trabaja en una oficina.}} {{Mis amigos y yo practicamos fútbol los martes.}} {{Mi hermano no canta, pero toca la guitarra.}} {{Los sábados mis abuelos bailan en la cocina.}}","placeholder":"Yo estudio…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 5 sentences","sentences":5},{"t":"A **yo** form (-o)","any":["hablo","estudio","trabajo","escucho","bailo","canto","toco","miro","necesito","llego","tomo","camino","practico","nado","compro","uso","busco","preparo","descanso","dibujo","monto","saco","ayudo","limpio","cocino","viajo","visito","llamo","enseño","juego"]},{"t":"A **nosotros** form (-amos)","re":"\\b\\p{L}+amos\\b"},{"t":"A **he / she / it** or **they** form","re":"\\b(habla|estudia|trabaja|escucha|baila|canta|toca|mira|necesita|llega|toma|camina|practica|nada|compra|usa|busca|prepara|descansa|dibuja|monta|saca|ayuda|limpia|cocina|viaja|visita|llama|enseña|hablan|estudian|trabajan|escuchan|bailan|cantan|tocan|miran|necesitan|llegan|toman|caminan|practican|nadan|compran|usan|buscan|preparan|descansan|dibujan|montan|sacan|ayudan|limpian|cocinan|viajan|visitan|llaman|enseñan)\\b"},{"t":"At least 5 different -ar verbs","any":["hablo","hablas","habla","hablamos","hablan","estudio","estudias","estudia","estudiamos","estudian","trabajo","trabajas","trabaja","trabajamos","trabajan","escucho","escuchas","escucha","escuchamos","escuchan","bailo","bailas","baila","bailamos","bailan","canto","cantas","canta","cantamos","cantan","toco","tocas","toca","tocamos","tocan","miro","miras","mira","miramos","miran","necesito","necesitas","necesita","necesitamos","necesitan","llego","llegas","llega","llegamos","llegan","tomo","tomas","toma","tomamos","toman","camino","caminas","camina","caminamos","caminan","practico","practicas","practica","practicamos","practican","nado","nadas","nada","nadamos","nadan","compro","compras","compra","compramos","compran","preparo","prepara","preparamos","preparan","descanso","descansa","descansamos","descansan","dibujo","dibuja","dibujamos","dibujan","ayudo","ayuda","ayudamos","ayudan","cocino","cocina","cocinamos","cocinan","visito","visita","visitamos","visitan","llamo","llama","llamamos","llaman","uso","usa","usamos","usan","busco","busca","buscamos","buscan","limpio","limpia","limpiamos","limpian"],"min":5}]},"reflect":{"q":"Salamanca's students have studied there for 800 years, and many came from far away to learn. Who helps *you* learn: a teacher, a parent, a friend, a coach? What does that person do that helps, and how could you do the same for someone else?","placeholder":"Someone who helps me learn is…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"errors","title":"Challenge: fix the mistakes","intro":"Each sentence has one wrong word. Tap it, then type the correct word.","items":[{"s":"Nosotros habla español en clase.","bad":"habla","fix":"hablamos","why":"*Nosotros* → -amos."},{"s":"Yo escucha la radio.","bad":"escucha","fix":"escucho","why":"*Yo* → -o."},{"s":"Mis primos trabajamos en una tienda.","bad":"trabajamos","fix":"trabajan","why":"*Mis primos* = ellos → -an."},{"s":"Tú miro la televisión.","bad":"miro","fix":"miras","why":"*Tú* → -as."},{"s":"Ellas canta en el coro.","bad":"canta","fix":"cantan","why":"*Ellas* → -an."}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** In Salamanca, students who graduated used to celebrate by painting their names on the university walls in red paint. Some of those painted names are still there, hundreds of years later.","unitTitle":"Mi vida diaria: el presente","code":"ODEyMS1BQ05BTUFMQVM=","prev":"m10-familia-posesivos.html","next":"m12-verbos-er-ir.html"});
